 ### [Spherical Voxel Grid Setup](3883-spherical-voxel-grid-setup.md)
-Spherical Voxel Grid Setup initializes the data structures required for efficient ray casting traversal within a spherical coordinate volume. It computes the discretization steps, precomputes trigonometric values, and constructs geometric primitives (line segments) that define voxel boundaries, enabling the `walkSphericalVolume` algorithm to determine ray-voxel intersections without repeated expensive trigonometric calculations or square roots during the rendering pass. It differs from Cartesian voxel grid setups by operating in a $(r, \theta, \phi)$ coordinate system tailored for egocentric view synthesis, where resolution requirements are anisotropic and radial distances vary significantly [3883-spherical-voxel-grid-setup.md].
